200 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (Acting as a mediator between Model objects and View objects in an application is a Controller object. There is usually one per application or window. A Controller object communicates data back and forth between the Model objects and the View objects. Since what a Controller does is very specific to an application, it is generally not reusable even though it often comprises much of an application's code.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
201 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (Because of the Controller's central mediating role, Model objects need not know about the state and events of the user interface, and View objects need not know about the programmatic interfaces of the Model objects.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
